ABBA: The Movie is a 1977 mockumentary comedy-drama film about the
1977 Australian tour by the Swedish pop group ABBA.

11
01:01:28,235 --> 01:01:34,235
An international co-production between Sweden and Australia, the film was directed
by Lasse Hallström, who previously helmed most of the band's videos.

12
01:07:03,529 --> 01:07:09,529
Its release coincided with ABBA: The Album, the group's fifth studio album, and features many songs from that album
as well as many of their earlier hits, and one, "Get on the Carousel", unavailable anywhere else.

13
01:12:38,823 --> 01:12:44,823
Theatrically released in December 1977 in Sweden and Australia,
it made its way overseas throughout 1978–79.

14
01:18:14,117 --> 01:18:20,117
The film was a box office success and received positive reviews from
critics, while gaining an enthusiastic response from ABBA fans.

15
01:23:49,411 --> 01:23:55,411
The film explores themes of pop music, music tour,
international relations, music documentary, pop band.

16
01:29:24,705 --> 01:29:30,705
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
